Save Data (Persistence)
You can easily persist player data (e.g. scores & progress) using the Save functions. Saved data will persist even when the player leaves your game. You can **only** call these methods from the server. If you need them on the client you'll need to use an RPC or SyncVar to push them down. 

To share data between multiple games You can set a "parent game ID" on the website. All games with a parent game ID will store their data on the parent. All calls to get data in your game will pull it from the parent game.

Player Data
Each player has their own "Save" that you can interact with by setting strings or ints with Save.SetInt or Save.SetString. These methods take a player as the first parameter, a key and a value, and then a default parameter.

Game Data
The Game scoped endpoints are for storing game-wide config (e.g. level XP requirements or message of the day notifications) e.g. Save.SetGameString

Ordered Player Data (Leaderboards)
Save.Ordered* and Leaderboard methods allow you to interact with and query sorted data for your player, for example scores or levels. See Leaderboards for more info

You can also view data saved about your game and players from the Create tab of the website under the "Manage Data" button